{"name":"Takaka","hex":"#3d4d78","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Takaka","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A small town in Golden Bay, Tasman district, South Island, New Zealand.","A river in Tasman district, New Zealand which passes through the town."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Takaka"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tākaka","blocks":[{"text":"Tākaka is a small town situated at the southeastern end of Golden Bay, at the northern end of New Zealand's South Island, located on the lower reaches of the Tākaka River. State Highway 60 runs through Takaka and follows the river valley before climbing over Tākaka Hill, to Motueka linking Golden Bay with the more populated coast of Tasman Bay to the southeast. The town is served by Tākaka Aerodrome."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Takaka_Commercial_Street_003.JPG/330px-Takaka_Commercial_Street_003.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/T%C4%81kaka","wikidata":"Q151841"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Lake_Killarney_7063_01.jpg/500px-Lake_Killarney_7063_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Lake_Killarney_7063_01.jpg/1280px-Lake_Killarney_7063_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Lake_Killarney_7063_01.jpg/500px-Lake_Killarney_7063_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lake Killarney","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALake_Killarney_7063_01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Takaka_Fonterra_Dairy_Factory.jpg/500px-Takaka_Fonterra_Dairy_Factory.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1